<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pajaritos port still closed, seen opening.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pajaritos port still closed, seen opening.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican crude port Pajaritos remained closed to shipping Friday although it should re-open later in the day, a port official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still closed, but it looks like we will be opening later,&quot; the official said. She added she was unable to specify a time.</p>
<p>Pajaritos was shut 1230 local/1830 GMT on Thursday because of high winds. The port ships an average 399,000 barrels per day of crude.</p>
<p>Dos Bocas, Mexico's other crude port susceptible to temporary winter closures, remained open, an official there said Friday.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
